          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تفریح (tafrih) — \"recreation, fun; an outing\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "آخر هفته برای تفریح به کوه میرویم. âkhar-e hafte barâ-ye tafrih be kuh miravim. At the weekend we go to the mountains for fun."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "tafrih kardan — to have fun, to go on an outing. Plural tafrihât."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "tafrih comes from Arabic tafrīḥ (EtymDB), a word usually glossed 'cheering up, gladdening'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
