              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "سرگرم شدن (sargarm shodan) — \"to be absorbed (in); to be entertained\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بچه ها با بازی سرگرم شدند. bachchehâ bâ bâzi sargarm shodand. The children got absorbed in the game."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "sargarm 'busy, absorbed' (sar 'head' + garm 'warm') + shodan. sargarmi is a hobby."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "sargarm shodan is built on inherited words: sar, 'head', and garm, 'warm', which EtymDB traces back to a Proto-Indo-European root meaning 'to heat' (EtymDB), and shodan, 'to become': a warm head, busy with something."
            }
          ]
        },
